-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Worldforged pickups: the items no pickup object hands out
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- `2026_09_16_00_worldforged_pickups.sql` restores the pickups the realm's own
-- catalog knows: an object, the item its loot row names, and one position. An item
-- the catalog never gave an object to has no pickup at all, however often the
-- community recorded it on the ground.
--
-- This migration creates that object. The archive's pins are the source: a pin
-- carries the item, the zone, the map and the position the item was looted at, on
-- Conquest of Azeroth, at least twice-confirmed. An item pinned in several zones is
-- a pickup in each of them, which is what the pins are.
--
-- WHERE EVERY VALUE COMES FROM
--   item     the pin's own item, and no other pickup in the database hands it out:
--            not a creature's loot, a reference loot, a vendor, a quest reward or a
--            container - checked before the gap list was drawn
--   name     the item's own name, as the realm's pickups are named after their item
--   display  the CoA catalogue's own appearance for that object where it holds one,
--            otherwise the appearance this restoration already gives an item of the
--            same class and subclass, otherwise the prop it falls back to elsewhere;
--            every id is one the client's GameObjectDisplayInfo can load
--   size     the size the realm's own pickups use, and the same lock
--   position the pin's own X and Y in the pin's own zone
--   height   the height of the nearest object the realm already has on that map, so
--            a pickup stands inside the same room, cave or camp, not at sea level
--
-- Mystic Scrolls are deliberately not included: they are a separate family and
-- nothing in the evidence ties them to a pickup object.
--
-- Idempotent: the entry range and the guid range are cleared by their own bounds
-- first. Apply to acore_world.
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

START TRANSACTION;

-- Clear this migration's own bounds, so re-applying it never doubles a pickup.
DELETE FROM `gameobject_loot_template` WHERE `Entry` BETWEEN 1345000 AND 1345999;
DELETE FROM `gameobject_template`      WHERE `entry` BETWEEN 1345000 AND 1345999;
DELETE FROM `gameobject`               WHERE `guid`  BETWEEN 6910001 AND 6919999;

-- The pickup objects, one per item, in an entry range nothing else uses.

-- Each object holds its item, at the chance the restoration's own pickups use.

-- 461 spawns: one per pinned zone, at the pin's own position, with the height of the
-- nearest object the realm already has on that map.

COMMIT;
